Description:

Fixes for UTF8=ACCEPT and IMAP4rev2 mailbox names.  imapd no longer
crashes on a mailbox name that isn't UTF-8, and rejects malformed UTF-8 in
quoted strings and atoms with BAD (RFC 9755).  Every command now finds a
mailbox by any Unicode normalization form of its name, not just CREATE,
SELECT, DELETE and RENAME.  New mailbox names may no longer contain C1
control characters, U+2028, U+2029 or unpaired surrogates.


